T {[S] start-up} 325 -1150 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {m = 8: Q2 = 8 x Q1} 825 -220 0 0 0.25 0.25 {}
T {[R] output, I_ref} 1085 -1150 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[C] bandgap core} 625 -1150 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[8] PMOS diodes, NMOS sinks} 1525 -1150 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[8] vabp} 1365 -1150 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[8] PMOS sources, NMOS diodes} 2005 -1150 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[8] vabn} 1845 -1150 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {bias_bg_pd: self-contained bias, current-mode bandgap with pnpMPA and rhigh + mirror tree of d2s_bias_in, digital enable en_3v3} 130 -1230 0 0 0.5 0.5 {}
T {branch current V_BE1/R1 + U_T ln 8 / R0 = 2.5 uA; I_ref = 2 x branch = 5 uA into NI (through TGN / TGP); Q1 / Q2: emitter 2u x 2u} 130 -1180 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {bg_core: current-mode (Banba type) bandgap, no op-amp.} 1280 -80 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   The PMOS mirror makes both branch currents equal and the NMOS pair NA / NB (gates on g) forces ea = eb, so each} 1280 -56 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   branch carries V_BE1 / R1 + U_T ln 8 / R0 (Q2 = 8 x Q1). rhigh (-0.22 %/K) nearly cancels V_BE's -1.77 mV/K already,} 1280 -32 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   so the PTAT share through R0 is small. PO / POC deliver twice the branch current, 5 uA, into NI.} 1280 -8 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   R1A is 10 % longer than R1B: with both PNPs off the loop gain is then > 1, so the core cannot rest there.} 1280 16 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   PB / PBC are stacked diodes; the PMOS run in moderate inversion for headroom at 3.0 V, ss, -40 C.} 1280 40 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {Mirror tree and diodes. The four diodes are those of d2s_bias_lp without the class-AB stacks and set the bias voltages:} 1280 64 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   vbp: BP 5u/6u, 5 uA (unit tails).  vbpc: BPC 1u/4u, 2 uA (mirror cascodes).  vabp: 5 uA out to RP2 on RP1 (ABP, FPL).} 1280 88 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   vbn: BN 6u/6u, 5 uA (fold sinks).  vbnc: BNC 1u/8u, 2 uA (fold cascodes).  vabn: 5 uA out to RN2 on RN1 (ABN, FNL).} 1280 112 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {PMOS gate lines come from PMOS diodes on vdd, NMOS gate lines from NMOS diodes on vss: bias crosses blocks as currents.} 1280 136 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {The class-AB stacks RP1 + RP2 / RN1 + RN2 (RP1 / RN1 replicas of OP / ON, nets dabp / dabn) moved to the pad (RP2 / RN2 in d2s_mpdda_pd, RP1 / RN1 in d2s_out_p / d2s_out_n since 2026-10-28)} 1280 160 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   on 2026-10-27: vabp / vabn are current outputs here; the CACE templates attach the stacks as fixtures.} 1280 184 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[E] enable} 145 -1150 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[E]} 388 -340 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[E]} 783 -1050 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[E] I_ref switch} 1215 -830 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[E] enable (en_3v3: 0 ... 3.3 V on vdd / vss, active high): IP / IN make en_3v3_b. Disabled: MS1 (gate now en_3v3_b instead of vss) is off,} 1280 208 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   SKS pulls ks to vss and SVPG pulls vpg to vdd, so the core stays off; TGN / TGP cut the core output iref off NI, and TDN pulls ni to vss.} 1280 232 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {   Enabled: these switches are off, MS1 conducts as before and the core starts.} 1280 256 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
T {[E]} 1108 -340 0 0 0.3 0.3 {layer=10}
